# Capability YAML is checked out with LF on every platform. Two starter files
# are embedded into the binary with include_str! (src/commands/mod.rs), so a
# Windows build from a CRLF checkout would ship them with CRLF bytes. The pin
# hash reads CRLF as LF either way (src/capability/hash.rs); this keeps the
# embedded bytes identical across release targets.
capabilities/**/*.yaml text eol=lf
